From: giteaguy <73799093+irnutsmurt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 15:35:51 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] cellSaveData: the save list's time read through glibc's
 timespec on Linux

dotheroes M11.4. pick_describe (the save-data list, 0131/0139) read st.st_mtime, which this file undefines on
glibc (the macro collides with CellSaveData*Stat's members): the Linux build stopped there. It reads st_mtim.tv_sec
as the file's other POSIX branches do (st_mtimespec on Darwin); Windows unchanged.
---
 libs/system/cellSaveData.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libs/system/cellSaveData.c b/libs/system/cellSaveData.c
index d76c943d..fdd1f76e 100644
--- a/libs/system/cellSaveData.c
+++ b/libs/system/cellSaveData.c
@@ -1237,7 +1237,13 @@ static void pick_describe(SavePick* e)
     char path[1024];
     snprintf(path, sizeof path, "%s/%s/PARAM.SFO", s_save_root, e->dir);
     struct stat st;
+#ifdef _WIN32
     e->mtime = stat(path, &st) == 0 ? (long long)st.st_mtime : 0;
+#elif defined(__APPLE__)
+    e->mtime = stat(path, &st) == 0 ? (long long)st.st_mtimespec.tv_sec : 0;
+#else   /* glibc's st_mtime macro is undefined above: its timespec field */
+    e->mtime = stat(path, &st) == 0 ? (long long)st.st_mtim.tv_sec : 0;
+#endif
     char when[32] = "";
     if (e->mtime) {
         time_t t = (time_t)e->mtime;
-- 
